// U7 L3 Quiz

::U7 L3 Quiz Q01::A campaign goal is “help everyone be healthier.” What is the main weakness? {=It lacks a specific audience, behavior, timeframe, and measure.~It is too measurable.~It identifies too many sources.~It contains too much accessibility information.}

::U7 L3 Quiz Q02::Which call to action is most usable? {=Refill your bottle at the station beside the library entrance today.~Care more about hydration.~Make better choices someday.~Everyone should change.}

::U7 L3 Quiz Q03::Why use plain language in health communication? {=It improves comprehension and action without sacrificing accuracy.~It guarantees agreement.~It removes the need for evidence.~It targets only young children.}

::U7 L3 Quiz Q04::A flyer uses tiny pale text. Which principle is violated? {=Accessibility.~Corroboration.~Random sampling.~Confidentiality of a dataset.}

::U7 L3 Quiz Q05::Which message avoids stigmatizing framing? {=Describe the barrier and available support without blaming affected people.~Label people by a health condition.~Use fear and shame to force action.~Assume behavior reflects character.}

::U7 L3 Quiz Q06::Why identify a decision-maker in advocacy? {=The requested change must reach someone able to authorize or influence it.~It makes evidence unnecessary.~Only elected officials make decisions.~It guarantees success.}

::U7 L3 Quiz Q07::What is the best evidence that a communication campaign worked? {=A predefined audience behavior or comprehension measure improved.~The designer likes the poster.~The message uses many colors.~The campaign was expensive.}

::U7 L3 Quiz Q08::A message says “studies prove” but lists no source. Best revision? {=Name and link the relevant credible evidence and represent its limits.~Add an exclamation point.~Remove all uncertainty words.~Replace evidence with a testimonial.}

::U7 L3 Quiz Q09::Why test a draft with members of the intended audience? {=They can identify unclear wording, barriers, and unintended interpretations.~They will always approve it.~Testing proves the health claim.~Only experts can notice confusion.}

::U7 L3 Quiz Q10::Which advocacy request is most feasible? {=Ask the school to add clearly labeled water-refill signs at two entrances.~Demand that all health disparities end tomorrow.~Ask no specific person for no specific action.~Request a change unrelated to the evidence.}

